{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And every wise-hearted one among the makers of the work made.</b> The wisest among them made the Mishkan, which was skilled work upon diverse forms from both its sides, as the Sages of blessed memory mentioned (Yoma 72b), and the curtains were not thick like the parochet. And he repeats in this passage everything stated above in the command in the section of Terumah, to make known that they made everything with intent to do according to the will of the one who commanded and toward his end. And the Ark, which was the most distinguished of the vessels, was made by Betzalel, who was the greatest of them all, as they said of blessed memory (Berakhot 55a): Betzalel knew how to combine the letters with which heaven and earth were created."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:22.278969985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}